// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO2 (ETH_PHY_POWER), GPIO14 (ETH_PHY_MDIO),
// and GPIO19/21/22/25/26/27 (standard ESP32 EMAC RMII data pins, fixed
// silicon pins for the onboard DP83848 Ethernet PHY - none of these are
// aliased anywhere in this board's own pins_arduino.h, confirming full
// dedication). GPIO16/17 (MDC / clock out) are already absent from the
// ESP32-classic chip default (PSRAM-reserved range).
//
// pfodWeb NOTE (button/LED capability-tagging pass): GPIO18
// (LED_BUILTIN in this board's pins_arduino.h) is confirmed as a real
// onboard LED - it is the vendor's own declaration, submitted directly
// into the official Espressif arduino-esp32 core (PR #5269, "Trueverit
// Universal IoT Driver MK II"). However, no independent source could be
// found anywhere (espboards.dev, PlatformIO's board docs, the GitHub PR
// discussion thread, trueverit.com's product pages, or any
// schematic/datasheet) confirming the LED's actual polarity - every
// reachable source is either silent on the point or is itself just a
// re-derivation of this same pins_arduino.h file. Per this pass's
// "never guess" policy, NO led_high/led_low tag was applied; GPIO18
// keeps its plain digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output capabilities
// only (chipGpios entry below left unchanged). No onboard button or
// relay-output GPIO could be identified from any source either - this
// OEM industrial board has essentially no public pin-level
// documentation beyond the vendor-submitted variant file itself (per
// playbook policy, relay outputs are KEEP not excludable regardless,
// but there was no GPIO to identify as relay-specific in the first
// place). See notes.txt for the full source list.
//
// One real bug WAS found and fixed this pass: `SCK = 18` in
// pins_arduino.h collided with the confirmed LED pin (GPIO18) -
// build_boards.js would have unconditionally appended an spi_sck
// capability onto the LED's GPIO regardless of this file's chipGpios
// map, since that alias-collision check runs independent of any
// override here. The SCK alias was deleted from pins_arduino.h
// (SS/MOSI/MISO left as-is - no collision found for those three) with
// an explanatory NOTE added there; see notes.txt.
